## The verdict on the line is not trusted

Emitting a claim is not checking it. `verify/witness/WitnessCheck.lean` is the second decider: it parses the committed corpus and re-derives every verdict from the evidence fields alone — a `wp` line must carry its site digest in `rm`, a `gc` line must be exactly the singleton `{site}`, a `matched-only` obligation must justify every collateral removal with a fired invocation, the census must equal the count of lines it claims to count. A line whose fields disagree with its verdict rejects, even though the compiler printed it.

The gate (`scripts/witness_gate.sh`) runs three corpora: golden (47 lines, every verdict must re-match), forged (66 lines, every one must reject — a checker that accepts a forged witness is a red battery, not a caveat), and drift (duplicate and count-drifted lines must fail the batch as accounting violations, not pass silently). No `WITNESS_CHECK` marker, no enforce, no corpus — and an empty corpus *fails* the gate rather than passing vacuously. A missing Lean toolchain is a `FAIL` naming the path, never a skip.

