## Why this shape

Proof-carrying code's viability rested on the certifying compiler: Touchstone generated the proofs automatically because nobody would hand-write them. The same accounting applies here — the producer (the auto-discharge solver, the transform runner) is untrusted; the witness is data; the checker's verdict is the only one that counts. Solver ≠ checker, and disagreement refuses naming both. What the witness channel adds to the 1997 shape: the corpus is *also* the conformance oracle. The Lean checker doesn't just verify claims — it detects when the Zig implementation drifts from the calculus it's supposed to implement, which is why forged and drift corpora are standing gates and not aspirational tests.
